From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Fri, 19 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: pinetab2: reserve memory for ramoops

The tablet has no reachable serial console, and with panic_on_oops and an
immediate panic reboot a kernel oops leaves no trace at all - the device
simply restarts. Reserve the region the Rockchip BSP uses for ramoops
(0x110000-0x1f0000, between the SCMI shared memory and the kernel) so
pstore can keep the oops and console output across the reboot.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi
@@ -78,6 +78,20 @@
 		regulator-max-microvolt = <1200000>;
 	};
 
+	reserved-memory {
+		/*
+		 * Same window the Rockchip BSP uses: after the SCMI shared
+		 * memory, before the kernel load address.
+		 */
+		ramoops@110000 {
+			compatible = "ramoops";
+			reg = <0x0 0x00110000 0x0 0x000e0000>;
+			record-size = <0x20000>;
+			console-size = <0x80000>;
+			pmsg-size = <0x20000>;
+		};
+	};
+
 	rk817-sound {
 		compatible = "simple-audio-card";
 		pinctrl-names = "default";
